## Spike pipeline — script execution order

| Step | Script | Purpose |
|------|--------|---------|
| 1 | `experiments_differential_ref_pairs.py` | Same as LFP — shared foundation |
| 2 | `common_ingest.py` | Same as LFP — shared foundation |
| 3 | `preprocessing_spikes.py` | Bandpass filter (300–6000 Hz) + threshold-based spike detection |
| 4a | `process_spikes_isi.py` | Inter-spike interval histograms per channel |
| 4b | `process_spikes_psth.py` | Peri-stimulus time histograms + firing rates |
| 5a | `postprocess_spikes_isi_mainfigure.py` | Group ISI + burst fraction Gardner-Altman plot |
| 5b | `postprocess_spikes_mua_firing_rate.py` | MUA firing rate as Gardner-Altman plots per channel with bootstrap CI |
| 5c | `postprocess_spikes_psth_supplement.py` | Full-epoch PSTH with maximum suppression |
| 5d | `postprocess_spikes_isi_supplement.py` | Full distribution ISI |


Steps 4 and 5 can be run in any order.

